# whose realised corner sits at about 0.66x the frequency requested, so every shaped edge in this
# library came out 1.55x (causal) or 2.10x (zero-phase) slower than the rise time asked for. The
# same defect had already been found and fixed in `instrument.scope_bandwidth`; the edge shaper
# never got the fix. Correcting it changes every waveform below, which is what this file is for:
# it caught the change, and these numbers are the deliberate break rather than a widened
# tolerance. `tests/test_edge_rise_time.py` is what stops it happening again.
